        "original_id": "4fb0447f-0cc3-54f0-b8bb-63950ca289a1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Yates, Italo Calvino, James Joyce\n- Works: Eleven Kinds of Loneliness, Liars in Love, Our Ancestors, Cosmicomics, Invisible Cities, If on a winter's night a traveler\n- Topics: short story collections, novels, literary comparisons\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Yates's first short story collection, Eleven Kinds of Loneliness, brought comparisons to James Joyce.\n- Italo Calvino's best known works include the Our Ancestors trilogy, published from 1952 to 1959.\n- Italo Calvino's best known works include the Cosmicomics short story collection, published in 1965.\n- Italo Calvino's best known works include the novel Invisible Cities, published in 1972.\n- Italo Calvino's best known works include the novel If on a winter's night a traveler, published in 1979.\n- Richard Yates published the short story collection Liars in Love in 1981.",
